  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "New HLA annotation, Indian variant, national database and 1000 Genomes hash resources broaden access to structured, reusable genomic data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reusable genomic infrastructure that turns variant-level data into structured resources for downstream analysis. hlafactor, a C++20 tool, standardises multi-layer functional annotation of HLA variation (tapasin dependency, expression, NK ligand groups) from two-field genotypes. GI-DB addresses underrepresentation of the Indian population in global genomic resources with a variant database reflecting its ethnolinguistic and biogeographical diversity. The CNCB-NGDC 2027 update adds thirteen new resources spanning genome variation and health and disease, among others. A preprint releases a public dataset of haploblock-based genomic hashes and clusters for 2,548 1000 Genomes individuals, generated with an optimized Genomic Cluster Engine pipeline for etiological subtyping. The items are heterogeneous in purpose; the shared novelty is expanded, standardised access rather than a single method.",
